{
  "doc": [
    "twoody/vault/computer-binding/v1 (docs/mesh-design.md §1, lot P0). Reference: src/vault/contracts.ts (signBinding, bindingValid).",
    "Signature scheme: exactly the v1 vault approval's (twoody-desktop src/shared/vault.ts signApproval, twoody-app utils/vault.js, twoody-backend VaultDevice#approval_message): Ed25519 (RFC 8032, deterministic) by the approving person-device's vault signing key — the private half of its vault_devices.sign_public — over the canonical header; signature = 64 bytes as 128 lowercase hex characters. Verified with the approver's sign_public taken from the verified roster (never from the binding).",
    "Canonical header: UTF-8 bytes of the label 'twoody/vault/computer-binding/v1' (no separator), then for each field in order: the UTF-8 bytes of String(field), prefixed by their byte length as 2 bytes big-endian. Fields: [v, user_id, vault_device_id, account_computer_id, tunnel_public_key, pairing_public_key, can_approve].",
    "Field encodings: v = 1 → '1'; user_id = the account user id in decimal ('42'); vault_device_id = the vault_devices uuid (lowercase, dashed); account_computer_id = the account_computers uuid; tunnel_public_key = the computer's X25519 tunnel identity (src/tunnel/identity.ts), 32 bytes as 64 lowercase hex; pairing_public_key = its X25519 account pairing key (account_computers.public_key), 64 lowercase hex; can_approve = '1' or '0' (never 'true'/'false').",
    "Wire form (what the backend stores next to the vault device and returns in GET /vault): {vault_device_id, account_computer_id, tunnel_public_key, pairing_public_key, can_approve: JSON boolean, approver_id: the signing vault device id, signature}. user_id is implied by the account.",
    "Rules for verifiers: the approver must be a trusted member of the verified roster whose own binding, if it has one, says can_approve=true; a binding signed by the bound device itself, or by any device whose binding says can_approve=false, is refused; a computer (Pi, NAS) always has can_approve=false, a Desktop with someone at the screen may have true. Clients refuse approvals and epoch envelopes from a device whose binding says can_approve=false.",
    "Keys: the private halves below are test keys, derived as SHA-256('twoody/p0/fixture/<name>'). Ed25519 private = 32-byte seed (what @noble/curves and OpenSSL raw keys take).",
    "approval_v1_same_key: the ordinary v1 approval of the Pi's vault device by the same iPhone key, cross-checked with twoody-desktop and twoody-app approvalValid — the binding uses the same key and the same encoding."
  ],
